<title>UK: United News up as SBC Warburg rates &quot;buy&quot;.</title>
<headline>United News up as SBC Warburg rates &quot;buy&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in United News &amp; Media Plc jumped on Thursday after analysts at SBC Warburg reiterated a &quot;buy&quot; recommendation on the stock, market sources said.</p>
<p>By 1147 GMT the stock was up 16-1/2p at 676-1/2, extending a rebound since it closed at a four-month low of 647p on December 13.</p>
<p>Sources said the broker had marginally downgraded its 1996 profit estimates for the publishing group on currency effects, but nevertheless remained positive on the stock.</p>
<p>-- Jennifer Scott, London newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
